# Lava Burst's damage to a creature can't be dealt instead to another permanent or player; its damage to a player can (its
# rulings; CR 614.9). Bot1 casts Lava Burst with X 1 at its own Ornithopter, and Bot2 answers with Reverberation ("all damage
# that would be dealt this turn by target sorcery spell is dealt to that spell's controller instead"): the Ornithopter is
# dealt the 1 damage and Bot1 none. Bot1's second Lava Burst, X 2 at Bot2, meets a second Reverberation and is dealt to
# Bot1 instead.

